400, NOT A CLAMP: HTTP 400 invalid_request_error with 'invalid temperature: only 1 is allowed for this model' or '… only 0.6 is allowed …' (github cline/cline#10544 2026-05-04; HKUDS/nanobot#4961; MoonshotAI/kimi-cli#1924 2026-04-17; lobe-chat#14122; promptfoo moonshot docs). Kimi's errors page maps invalid parameters to 400 invalid_request_error.
MoonshotAnthropic: the Messages API schema (docs/api/messages.md, same date) has NO temperature property at all and documents only kimi-k3. Whether /anthropic 400s or ignores a temperature is NOT documented. Assume the same backend validation. Omitting the field is always safe because the value is fixed server-side.
CAUTION ON THE ADR 0025 SHAPE: 'temperature=1 passes' is WRONG for kimi-k2.6 non-thinking, where 1 gets a 400 and only 0.6 is accepted. Moonshot cannot send thinking:{type:disabled} today (reasoning_effort is cleared on K2), so this is latent, but it becomes real once k215 or a thinking mapping lands. Also, unlike OpenAI the rejection does not depend on effort, so ADR 0025's runtime, effort-aware predicate is overkill.
RECOMMEND: (1) A static per-model clear (ADR 0019 layer 3) on BOTH faces: 'kimi-k3' => {…, temperature=>0}, qr/\Akimi-k2(?!\d)/ => {…, temperature=>0}. That covers k2.6, k2.7-code(-highspeed), k2.5 and k2-thinking. Never emit temperature on any current Kimi id, including 1. (2) Get the drop+carp in one shared place: in both _temperature_kwargs gates (Role::OpenAICompatible, Role::AnthropicCompatible), when a caller-set temperature is present, != 1 and supports('temperature') is false, carp 'dropping temperature=X: model fixes it server-side'. The same carp then also covers Anthropic Opus 4.7+ (k138 clear), which is silent today. That behavior change needs an ADR 0025 Update. (3) Do not match OpenRouter's moonshotai/kimi-* (aggregator, unchecked). (4) Tests: a request-building test that k3, k2.6 and k2.7-code send no temperature at 0.7 or at 1, and that the carp fires only for != 1.

